  "docTitle": "Proximity Service & Nearby Friends (Yelp) - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design a proximity service (Yelp: restaurants near me) and a nearby-friends feature: geohash, quadtree, S2 and H3, read-heavy business index, moving-location updates over WebSocket and pub/sub, from a kid story to interview answers.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">35 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Google</span><span class=\"chip company\">Uber</span><span class=\"chip company\">Meta</span><span class=\"chip company\">Amazon</span><span class=\"chip company\">Swiggy / Zomato</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Proximity Service &amp; Nearby Friends (Yelp)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">\"Show me restaurants within 2 km\" and \"show me which friends are near me right now\" look like the same question. They are not. One searches 200 million places that almost never move. The other tracks millions of phones that move every few seconds. After this page you can design both, pick between geohash, quadtree, S2 and H3 with a reason, and do the numbers on a whiteboard.</p>\n      "
  },
